{"type":"thought","data":" targets today when "}
{"type":"thought","data":"not governed, but the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" spec requires the operator-decided"}
{"type":"thought","data":" root exception."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe spec’s root refusal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" applies before any "}
{"type":"thought","data":"state lookup, so it "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is not governed by the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" phase gate. G-3’s governed-only"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rule would wrongly "}
{"type":"thought","data":"allow a mode 000 root."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The spec explicitly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" separates absent, non-directory,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and non-traversable"}
{"type":"thought","data":" roots into a separate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" refusal path."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe root-cannot-be-entered"}
{"type":"thought","data":" refusal is absent from"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the plan, so FR-3 is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" classified as restated"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rather than a direct"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contradiction. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"task-ordering and kind-contradiction"}
{"type":"thought","data":" findings are must-fix."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan lists deliverable"}
{"type":"thought","data":" D-10 before D-9. This"}
{"type":"thought","data":" ordering is a nit.\n\n"}
{"type":"thought","data":"T12 depends on T11 and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" T11 on T10. Both T7"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and T12 edit the same"}
{"type":"thought","data":" adapter files. T7 re-checks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" them but delegates "}
{"type":"thought","data":"their oracle line to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" T12. This overlap risks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" conflicting edits."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe scope list correctly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" includes the three "}
{"type":"thought","data":"runtime markdown files."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan claims `ArgumentParser`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is defined inside `main`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and that five `add_argument`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" calls exist. This must"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be verified at SHA "}
{"type":"thought","data":"644f8bf6 or the current"}
{"type":"thought","data":" commit.\n\nThe plan also"}
{"type":"thought","data":" claims Python 3.9.6"}
{"type":"thought","data":" supports `O_SEARCH`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" while 3.11.8 does not."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The effort contract"}
{"type":"thought","data":" requires executing "}
{"type":"thought","data":"such premises, so the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" audit will check whether"}
{"type":"thought","data":" those interpreter versions"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are installed."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe audit will not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" run pytest at commit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 983c2f85 to verify "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the published test count"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of 4618. That would"}
{"type":"thought","data":" require a writeable"}
{"type":"thought","data":" worktree, which violates"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the instruction to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"avoid editing or creating"}
{"type":"thought","data":" files outside the working"}
{"type":"thought","data":" directory."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe audit will verify"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the anchor check claim"}
{"type":"thought","data":" by running `git show`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and `git grep`, which"}
{"type":"thought","data":" do not create files."}
{"type":"thought","data":" It will also compare"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the current HEAD against"}
{"type":"thought","data":" commit 983c2f85 to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"confirm the tree matches"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the published baseline"}
{"type":"thought","data":" before running the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"read-only anchor check."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The approved set key"}
{"type":"thought","data":" spelling in `compare_readings`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is consistent between"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the plan and the spec."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nManual rows in T0 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"cannot hide softening"}
{"type":"thought","data":" because they are not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" compare_readings keys."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe agent CLI claim"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that every subprocess"}
{"type":"thought","data":" gets a constructed "}
{"type":"thought","data":"PATH may exclude git."}
{"type":"thought","data":" T10 tests AC-8.3 and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" AC-8.4, which require"}
{"type":"thought","data":" git on PATH, but the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan's private-bin-only"}
{"type":"thought","data":" PATH might omit it."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe blanket PATH rule"}
{"type":"thought","data":" likely over-constrains"}
{"type":"thought","data":" AC-8.3, since that "}
{"type":"thought","data":"test requires git on"}
{"type":"thought","data":" PATH while AC-8.4 uses"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a PATH without git."}
{"type":"thought","data":" On macOS, git is probably"}
{"type":"thought","data":" present in /usr/bin,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" so the risk is minimal."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe agent CLI PATH"}
{"type":"thought","data":" concern is resolved:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the blanket rule applies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to subprocesses, not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to git itself. AC-8.4's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" hermetic PATH without"}
{"type":"thought","data":" git is a valid exception."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nT10's ten-second subprocess"}
{"type":"thought","data":" timeout for git rev-parse"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a sound implementation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" detail.\n\nThe audit "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is now examining whether"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Claude's gate Python"}
{"type":"thought","data":" call replaces `pwd "}
{"type":"thought","data":"-P` and correctly handles"}
{"type":"thought","data":" M:H11."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe spec allows at"}
{"type":"thought","data":" most one added Python"}
{"type":"thought","data":" process, so the plan's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" single call replacing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" both `ROOT_ABS` and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `M:H11` is acceptable."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The audit is now checking"}
{"type":"thought","data":" whether that call precedes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the state read. T3 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"places the FR-3 refusal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" after `_read_state`,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but the spec requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" canonicalisation before"}
{"type":"thought","data":" any exemption. If the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan omits an ordering"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rule, the implementer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" might use a non-canonical"}
{"type":"thought","data":" root for state lookup."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe spec requires "}
{"type":"thought","data":"canonicalisation before"}
{"type":"thought","data":" any state lookup. T3"}
{"type":"thought","data":" places the FR-3 refusal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" after `_read_state`,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" which is vague but "}
